@baseUrl = https://localhost:7247

### 1. Prove Tenant A (Company 1) works
GET {{baseUrl}}/test-tenant/1

### 2. Register Tenant B company (check the returned companyId!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyCode": "COMP-B",
  "companyName": "Honey & Crumb Tenant B"
}

### 3. Link Tenant B to db80678 (replace companyId if not 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/company-databases
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 3,
  "serverName": "db80678.public.databaseasp.net,1433",
  "databaseName": "db80678",
  "credentialKey": "TenantB"
}

### 4. Register a device for Company 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": 1,
  "deviceCode": "POS-01",
  "deviceName": "Front Counter POS"
}

### 5. Add a product to Tenant A (Company 1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenant/1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productCode": "BRD-01",
  "productName": "Sourdough Loaf",
  "category": "Bread",
  "unitPrice": 180.00
}

### 6. Add a different product to Tenant B (Company 3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenant/3/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productCode": "CAK-01",
  "productName": "Honey Cake",
  "category": "Cakes",
  "unitPrice": 450.00
}

### 7. Verify isolation: Tenant A only shows Sourdough Loaf
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenant/1/products

### 8. Verify isolation: Tenant B only shows Honey Cake
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenant/3/products

### 9. Seed dev test users (run once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/seed-dev

### 10. Test login endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyCode": "COMP-A",
  "username": "owner1",
  "password": "Owner123!"
}